    "The only place that explained what I Don't Agree actually does was spoken by VoiceOver, not shown on screen — anyone reading the screen visually saw two buttons with no stated consequence for the second one. It now says so in plain text too: declining is fine, AppleVis stays fully browsable without signing in, and we'll ask again the next time you try to sign in. Discussed directly." : {
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "ar" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
